/* How the notices are meant to be used. Rendered on the readiness screens rather than only obeyed,
   because a rule nobody can read is a rule the next person breaks by accident. */
val capabilityRules = listOf(
    CapabilityRule("one-notice-per-screen",
        "A screen renders the notice for the capability it depends on. Not three of them stacked, and not one it does not use.",
        "A nurse's schedule carried a Design preview banner, a WORKSPACE · DEMO eyebrow and a Fictional workspace paragraph before any content — three sentences saying one thing, filling the screen above the first visit. A reader who is told the same thing three times has been told it none."),
    CapabilityRule("the-notice-is-the-contract",
        "No screen writes its own not-connected sentence. It names a capability and the sentence is rendered from this file.",
        "Sixty hand-typed variations cannot be switched off together, and some of them will be wrong. One place that knows means one boolean to change when an integration lands."),
    CapabilityRule("connected-needs-evidence",
        "A capability may be marked connected only when `evidence` names a file that exists and `blockedBy` is empty. The build refuses it otherwise.",
        "The failure mode is never a lie. It is somebody clearing a banner off a layout because the screenshot looked better without it."),
    CapabilityRule("scaffolding-is-not-a-disclosure",
        "A role switcher, a state picker and a gallery of loading states are development tools. They are removed from what ships, and removing them says nothing about whether anything is connected.",
        "The two got tangled: taking the demo furniture out felt like claiming the product was live. They are separate questions and this file answers only the second.")
